WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:06.120
One of the biggest challenges
that Asian-Americans face

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.010
is that they're behind the scenes.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.300
&gt;&gt; They don't wear
the passion on their sleeves.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.320
&gt;&gt; We don't put ourselves out there
enough, we're just not being seen for

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.880
executive positions.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.272
&gt;&gt; I don't think there is enough
Asian-American executives who are actually

00:00:19.272 --> 00:00:20.068
asking for help.

00:00:20.068 --> 00:00:23.357
[MUSIC]

00:00:23.357 --> 00:00:28.819
There exists different values
between Asian family tradition and

00:00:28.819 --> 00:00:32.270
American corporate culture system.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:36.100
&gt;&gt; Asian American executives have had
a reputation for technical competence.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.630
Their fundamental challenges
are a sense of invisibility,

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:43.720
leading teams, taking risks,
and speaking up.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.420
&gt;&gt; I look at the program as
providing an opportunity for

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:51.420
our attendees to be even more
successful in their jobs.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:58.210
&gt;&gt; It helped build my awareness about
the Asian tendencies that I have.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:02.710
I needed to do a better job at being
more visible with my accomplishments.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:07.630
&gt;&gt; The program opens my eyes to
this concept of managing up and

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.113
also exerting power.

00:01:09.113 --> 00:01:13.569
&gt;&gt; It gave you a different frame work
about how you need to think about business

00:01:13.569 --> 00:01:15.940
when you're at the upper tiers.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.590
&gt;&gt; It's really personal insights and

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:21.470
awareness in terms of what it takes to
be an executive at corporate levels.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.450
&gt;&gt; It's really improved my
effectiveness at the office,

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.720
improved my executive communications.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.010
&gt;&gt; The faculty are world class.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.480
They really believe in you and
they want you to succeed.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.060
&gt;&gt; The ALP program moved my
career from the C level staff for

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.480
a company in one of the hottest
areas in social analytics.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.560
&gt;&gt; I really believe that my recent
promotion was in part due to ALP.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.238
It gave me the tools and
skills I needed to be successful,

00:01:46.238 --> 00:01:49.316
not only in this position but
in my future ones.

